  "body": [
   "lap_net_status(${1:out})"
  ],
  "description": "int lap_net_status(lap_net_status_t *out)  All calls return immediately. Two outbound IPv4 sockets per app. No Wi-Fi credentials or join operation: first connect using LINK. Connect returns a handle >=0 or an error; poll state until CONNECTED or a negative error. Timeout (1..30000 ms) covers asynchronous DNS + connect, not stream lifetime. Host is DNS name or numeric IPv4, <=253 chars. IPv6/TLS/listening unsupported. send copies up to 4096 bytes into a bounded queue and returns bytes accepted (may be partial), EAGAIN if full/pending. Acceptance is not delivery. recv copies up to 4096 bytes, EAGAIN when empty/pending, 0 on peer EOF after queued bytes drain. Check negative errors; retry EAGAIN in later frames. Buffers/host/status must be app globals or app malloc allocations, not stack. Close invalidates the handle immediately; worker releases it asynchronously. Closing the app closes every socket and discards queued bytes.",
  "scope": "c"
 },
